diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 75de58e..29bbc8f 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 
 ## Unreleased
 
+- Compound units in results are written with a middle dot and superscript powers, as in `kg·m²/s²`; both forms are accepted as input.
 - `unitconv list` shows 20 units a page, with `--page N` and a `page N of M` footer.
 - `--json` output gives `unit` as an object with the unit's `symbol` and singular `name`.
 - Fixed: unit symbols in quantities were matched without regard to case, so `3 Mm` was read as millimetres. Symbols now match exactly; a symbol that matches only when case is ignored is refused with the spellings it might mean.
diff --git a/docs/reference.md b/docs/reference.md
index 5aae655..366d5f9 100644
--- a/docs/reference.md
+++ b/docs/reference.md
@@ -37,9 +37,9 @@ term that follows it, so `W/m^2/K` is watts per square metre per kelvin.
 
 | Fact | Value | Meaning |
 |---|---|---|
-| `unit.multiply` | `*` | joins units that multiply, as in `kg*m` |
+| `unit.multiply` | `·` | joins units that multiply in results, as in `kg·m`; input may also use `*` |
 | `unit.divide` | `/` | divides by the next unit, as in `m/s` |
-| `unit.power` | `^n` | raises a unit to an integer power, as in `s^2` or `s^-2` |
+| `unit.power` | `superscript` | integer powers are written as superscripts in results, as in `s²`; input may use them or `^`, as in `s^2` or `s^-2` |
 | `unit.reciprocal` | `1/` | a unit with nothing above the line, as in `1/s` |
 | `output.round_trip` | `yes` | every quantity unitconv prints is accepted back as input |
 | `mixed.separator` | `+` | a target such as `ft+in` gives whole feet and the remaining inches |
